# Protected paths: this file is the single source of truth for them.
# scripts/check-protected-paths.sh reads it to classify a diff as protected or unprotected,
# and `scripts/check-protected-paths.sh --validate` checks it. Use only the syntax that
# script's header documents. An agent never merges a PR that touches a protected path: one
# whose last matching line here has an owner. The one exception is a subtask PR into an epic
# branch whose plan allowed_paths cover the path (.claude/skills/tm-agent-loop/SKILL.md,
# "Merge conditions", condition 6). A line with no owner makes its path not owned
# (the later line wins, as on GitHub); only the four reference skill folders may have one.
# A pattern that matches no tracked file yet protects a file before it exists; --validate
# accepts that only for the patterns listed in scripts/check-protected-paths.py.

# Agent and repository configuration, docs that need the human's approval
/.github/                                   @ali-roozbahani
# Agent instructions and settings at any depth. Each unanchored line comes before the anchored
# root line it generalises, so a file protected before keeps its line.
.claude/                                    @ali-roozbahani
/.claude/                                   @ali-roozbahani
# Reference skills: not owned, so an agent may edit them and add files to them; the reviewer
# judges the diff and the rule-change signal escalates a removed or rewritten rule line. Whole
# folders, so a reference file added later needs no edit here. Only these four folders: a
# sibling skill folder and the rest of .claude/ stay protected by /.claude/. A CLAUDE.md or
# .gitignore inside one of them stays protected by the lines below, which come later.
/.claude/skills/tm-ios/
/.claude/skills/tm-android/
/.claude/skills/tm-kmp-shared/
/.claude/skills/tm-testing/
CLAUDE.md                                   @ali-roozbahani
/CLAUDE.md                                  @ali-roozbahani
CLAUDE.local.md                             @ali-roozbahani
.mcp.json                                   @ali-roozbahani
# Ignore files at any depth: the root one keeps local secrets and machine config out of git,
